tonic, which means that someone wants to engage in them. I liken it more, too, if you have a love of chocolate. You know, chocolate is really good until you have too much, right? And so, so it's more of an egosentonic, it kind of something that people want to do, whereas handwashing is something people hate doing that they feel compelled to do it. The medications for OCD do not across the board work for BFRBs. So that's a big difference. And then another difference is the treatments. And are, you know, there's some overlap, but there's also some real big differences. And what we don't want is for people to feel like medication doesn't work and treatment doesn't work. And maybe I could just add that as somebody who sort of come into the field relatively recently

